# lmkd needs to write cgroup.event_control, not just read the memcg files.
#
# It asks the kernel for PSI first and falls back to vmpressure when there is
# none -- and there is none here, PSI landed in 4.20 and this device runs
# 4.14.180. The fallback registers an eventfd by writing "<evfd> <mpfd> <level>"
# into /dev/memcg/cgroup.event_control; see init_mp_common in
# system/memory/lmkd/lmkd.cpp. AOSP grants lmkd only r_file_perms on cgroup
# files, because on a kernel new enough for PSI this path is never taken.
#
# Without it lmkd exits, init restarts it, and ActivityManagerService retries
# the connection from inside updateOomAdjLocked -- holding the AMS lock. That
# ends with the watchdog killing system_server: 7535 retries in one boot.
allow lmkd cgroup:file w_file_perms;
